Warning! Warning! Danger! Danger!
Confusion alert!

em86 is a package that allows linux/x86 programs to run under linux/AXP.
Wine is a package that allows Windows/x86 program to run under linux/x86.

It is highly unlikely that Wine will ever run under em86 ;-)
Also, although Wine/AXP (Running WindowsNT/AXP programs under linux/AXP)
has been talked about a lot, it has, to the best of my knowledge, never
progressed beyond that stage, and I don't expect it to ever do so.

As to what does or doesn't run on either --- I will leave that to people who
have more recent experience with those packages (mine are about a year
old, both cases).

