"Donald L. Baker" <dobak@ipa.net> writes:

> I'm interested in getting linux to run Fortran on my AlphaPC 164LX, 
> but I can't get Red Hat or the makers of Hard Hat to respond with 
> man pages on g77 and the associated debuggers so that I can check 
> out the capabilities.  In fact, I get no response at all, just like 
> Microsoft, DEC, IOMEGA and SyQuest.  It must be catching.  

I just installed RH 5.2 on my Pentium II, and it looks like RedHat
put egcs 1.0.3 into that release, but without including the g77 portions.
Looks offhand like all it supports is C and C++ (maybe Objective-C as
well).

It also looks like they installed the egcs documentation under man pages
and Info files named `egcs'.

I suggest using the CVS interface at <http://www.cygnus.com/egcs> to
find and grab the g77 documentation, or just ftp (from a similar
location) the g77 portion of the egcs distribution (for whatever
version you want, say 1.0.3 to be consistent, though 1.1 is out),
unpack that, and install the docs.  Note that the Info files are not
included, but their texinfo sources are, but if you just want the
(very short) man pages, it should be pretty easy to find and install
the relevant stuff.

I suspect RedHat 6.0, whenever it comes out, will include g77.  I'm
a bit surprised they didn't include it with 5.1 or especially 5.2 --
if not egcs-g77, they could have installed g77 0.5.23.

However, doing *that* would have required installing gcc 2.8, instead
of gcc 2.7.2.3, and they had *good* reasons to make sure gcc 2.7.2.3
was the default compiler -- namely, gcc 2.8 and Linux 2.0.* sources
don't work together (due to bugs hiding in Linux that gcc 2.8 exposes,
at least).  Same deal for egcs.

So RedHat didn't exactly commit an oversight here, IMO -- they were,
and will remain for awhile longer, a bit between a rock and a hard place.
There are various portions of the needed solutions coming (like, maybe
someday Linux 2.2.* will come out, a "stable" line that RH can use
and that gcc 2.8 and egcs can reliably compile), but I'm grateful RH
didn't wait for them to make RH 5.2.  :)
