Kap came up with this loop_unroll:

      subroutine MATMUL ( A, B, C, N )
       real A(N,N), B(N,N), C(N,N)
       integer N
       integer KII3, KII2, KII1
       do   I=1,N
        do   J=1,N
         A(I,J) = 0.
         KII2 = N - 7
         KII3 = (KII2 + 7) / 8
         KII1 = KII3 * 8 + 1
         do   K=1,KII2,8
          A(I,J) = A(I,J) + B(I,K) * C(K,J)
          A(I,J) = A(I,J) + B(I,K+1) * C(K+1,J)
          A(I,J) = A(I,J) + B(I,K+2) * C(K+2,J)
          A(I,J) = A(I,J) + B(I,K+3) * C(K+3,J)
          A(I,J) = A(I,J) + B(I,K+4) * C(K+4,J)
          A(I,J) = A(I,J) + B(I,K+5) * C(K+5,J)
          A(I,J) = A(I,J) + B(I,K+6) * C(K+6,J)
          A(I,J) = A(I,J) + B(I,K+7) * C(K+7,J)
         end do
         do   K=KII1,N,1
          A(I,J) = A(I,J) + B(I,K) * C(K,J)
         end do
        end do
       end do
    return
    end

Have to admit i never considered using the KAP
of this RS 6000 (wasn't even aware we actually have this)
so i'd think KAP can even do better, since this was just
a first clumsy test. Maybe it's actually capable of blocking ?
Dunno ?

Murx






