Yep, it seems to be a typing error.

I looked in the code and it seems that it has to be $f30 instead of $f3.
This way he checks if da equals zero, which essentually is a NOP for
xAXPY, so the code can return immediately.

$f3 usually is a register, that has to be retained from the calling
routine (the code does save it), and as long as it not happens to have a
value of zero by accident, the code worked.

Joachim Wesner



