As I'm sure you are aware, you've started with
the most common, but most inefficient, manner
of multiplying two matrices -- a complete
cache thrasher with poor data re-use.  My experience
with KAP long ago, gave me the impression that
KAP it is trained to recognize inefficient algorithms,
and replace them wholesale.

Simply reordering the loops up above, or transposing
one matrix first so columns are multiplied by
columns (instead of mixed column-row), will probably
give a factor 2 to 4 speed increase.  Some compilers
are smart enough to do that.



