Presumably it's not finding some libraries.  Go into sh and try:

> strace /usr/local/mozilla/bin/mozilla-SWim-for-RH4 2>&1 | grep lib   

or whatever.  You'll probably see a bunch of things like:

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
open("/lib/libnss_files.so.1.1", O_RDONLY) = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)
open("/usr/lib/libnss_files.so.1.1", O_RDONLY) = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)
open("/lib/libnss_nisplus.so.1.1", O_RDONLY) = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)
open("/usr/lib/libnss_nisplus.so.1.1", O_RDONLY) = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)
open("/lib/libnss_nis.so.1.1", O_RDONLY) = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)
open("/usr/lib/libnss_nis.so.1.1", O_RDONLY) = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)
open("/lib/libnss_dns.so.1.1", O_RDONLY) = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)
open("/usr/lib/libnss_dns.so.1.1", O_RDONLY) = -1 ENOENT (No such file or direct
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

depending on what's in your /etc/nsswitch.conf.  On RH5 it should be
finding these... perhaps you could just set LD_LIBRARY_PATH.

Back at the beginning of July I packaged up Kazushige's Mozilla with
the libraries it uses, to run it on RH4:

  http://pauillac.inria.fr/~harley/tmp/mozilla+extralibs.for.rh4.tar.gz

The Mozilla that's in there can also be replaced with the
11327480-byte mozilla-SWim-for-RH4 that Kazushige made.  Either works
fine for me.

