Xavier GALLEZ wrote:

> "-O4" is not a good option for DU. Try "-fast", it works much better.  

Just to be precise, the following is taken from `man f77`:

-fast  Sets the following command options that 
       can improve run-time performance: 
       -assume noaccuracy_sensitive, -align dcommons,
       -math_library fast, and -O4 (the default).

Two things to note

1) it also invokes -O4, so it can't be that bad
2) -O4 is default if you don't give any option to the 
compiler regarding optimization.

Christian



