From what I hear/read from other people that have actually looked in the
code, the whole thing is written in a pretty arcane style, i.e under the
old assumption that sizeof(int) = sizeof(pointer). This is an absolute
NOGO on an 64-Bit architecture. It seems that there a toooo many place,
where the above is used, that even Netscape itself is (for the moment)
not able to fix them all. The one Netscape that seems to run pretty well
on DU runs in a special 32-Bit mode, that does not (yet) work/exist
under Linux.

Joachim



