HI Folks,

I am pretty much wondering what kind of speed you are talking about if
you say NT would be dead slow. If you are talking about NT itself as a
operating system, you might be right. However, if you are talking about
execution time of computing applications it looks quite a bit different.
Eg. POVray 3 the well known raytracer. As a native alpha application
running under NT it takes POVray 20 seconds to render chess.pov at a
resolution of 640 x 480 with no antialiasing.
Compiled with EGCS under RH5.1 with the fast math librarys libfm-0.90
and libffm-0.21 it takes about 26 seconds to render the same picture
with the same POVray settings. On top of that, the Linux compile is very
unstable and generates a Floating Point exception if i try to render
skyvase.pov and dumps core.

My conclusion is if you have to do real computing work on an Alpha
machine you either get Windows NT, OR which I woud prefer of course
Digital Unix which compilers basically kick ass. I personally can't
afford DU because it is unfortunately f...ing expensive so that I am
stuck with Linux. Which, on the other hand is not so bad ;-)

