Just a sidenote, if you're a total Linux newbie, the Alpha platform is
not the best way to start, since most precompiled stuff (e.g. RPM's etc.
what you're looking for) are mainly  available for x86/Linux. 

Also, there are quite a bit 64bit unclean sources out there which
indeed won't/buggy compile on Alpha, so you'll have to tweak a bit
in the sources to them working. 

And last but not least, a lot of commercial packages like AppliX,
StarOffice et al are only available for Linux/x86. 

Alpha is a very nice platform if you already have some Linux/UNIX
experience (and preferable also some basic C coding skills)...

