I have no leads on rendering engines but can contribute to the thought
process.  POV-Ray is a true raytracer whereas, many other rendering engines use
scan-line rendering.  To the average Joe/Jane there isn't much difference but
to a graphic artist of even the most modest of standards the differences are
fairly visible.

Determine whether your happier with the results of one process or the other,
then search for engines that meet that standard.  

Look to newsgroups in the comp.graphics.rendering heirarchy for more discussion
of specific packages.

Keith.

