> I have the opportunity to buy the following graphics adapters:
> 
> * Diamond Fire GL 1000 Pro
> * Matrox Millenium II
> 
> Both 8 Mb. Which is preferable ? (in matter of speed)

The FireGL is faster in both 2D and 3D, that is,
ONLY when you use the MetroX server (about $39). 

The performance is rather poor with the SuSE XFree86 
GLINT server but it's very useable and stable.

You can even get a native FireGL OpenGL kit from MetroX,
although this will cost about $200 (great for Quake and
other 3D stuff) :)
 
> I know it's better to get Mettrolink for the Fire GL 1000 Pro
> how is the support for the Matrox Millenium II with XFree86 ?

The Millennium is about the fastest card you can get for
XFree86 and is speedwise very good supported (and is $0).

If you want both fast 2D and 3D get the FireGL, if you 
just want blazing 2D, get the Millennium since the 2D
speed difference is not that big and in real life usage
hardly noticable.

Regards,
Antoine



