This gray spirit wrote:

> Hello,
>
>         I am running RedHat 5.1 on a "Ruffian" (21164A/UX Alpha).  This is
> a report of my attempts to fix the broken configuration scripts for kernel
> compilation:
>
> 1. The kernel-2.0.35 compiles properly without any warnings. But it does
>    not work. On bootup, the machine simply freezes after milo uncompresses
>    the kernel and reports: "Now jumping to kernel ..."
>
> 2. Looking around, I saw several posts here claiming that make
> xconfig/menuconfig to be broken. So I reconfigured the kernel using make
> config using precisely the same options (A horrible, error-prone process).
> The resulting kernel runs!
>
> 3. To see what the difference was, "diff" was ran on the .config files
> produced in the configuration. There was only one "real" difference:
>
> CONFIG_VGA_CONSOLE=y
>
> was set in the config file for make config. In make xconfig, this define
> was not set.
>
> 4. This bug is related to the one where the VGA option cannot be turned on
> in xconfig. Looking at the tk scripts, it is not obvious what exactly is
> wrong with it. I have no experience with Tk/Tcl. Can someone with the
> relevant expertise check up on that, please?
>
> 5. Conclusion: You _can_ configure the kernel using xconfig. But the
> resulting .config file must be tweaked to add line CONFIG_VGA_CONSOLE=y
> _before_ we "make dep". I have recompiled the kernel with the
> method and it looks like it works.
>
> 6. As for why the tk widget for the VGA option is broken, that is still a
> mystery.
>
> I hope those who read this can incorporate this into the FAQs, and
> hopefully, fix this.
>
> Happy linuxing,
> css.



