Jack W. Crenshaw wrote:
[...]
> 
> Perhaps more to the point is, does the Alpha FP unit include trig
> functions, log, exp, etc., as  the Intel part does?  If so, there is
> nothing to be gained by trying to write one's own routines.

There is something to be gained for trig functions, as has
been discussed in comp.arch.  The x86 use a 66-bit approximation
of Pi, so when the argument of trig functions is large (thus
requires reduction to a pi/2 interval), accuracy is lost if
one uses the straight fcos and fsin.



