try doing this.

1. get the full kernel that you want to use (i.e. linux-2.0.36.tar.gz) from
ftp.kernel.org

2. move linux-2.0.36.tar.gz to the base of your source tree ( /usr/src/ )

3. cd /usr/src , the delete the old tree ( rm -rf linux  )

4. tar zxpvf linux-2.0.36.tar.gz

5. cd linux

6. change arch=alpha  and comment out the SMP=1 option in the Makefile

7. make menuconfig or xconfig ; then configure your kernel

8. make dep ; make clean

9. make boot

10. Test the kernel:  from milo prompt:
        MILO>boot sda1:/usr/src/linux/arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz
root=/dev/sda1  (if sda1 is not your boot partition change it to the one it
is.)

11. if it works, go back to /usr/src/linux/ and make modules ; make
modules_install

12. cd / ; then rename your vmlinux.gz to something else ( ie. mv
/vmlinux.gz /vmlinux.old.gz )

13 copy the new kernel to the root:
        cp /usr/src/linux/arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz /

14. that should be it.

NOTE: if you have an alphastation 200 4/233, there are other kernel tweaks
to fix
1. irq9 conflict with the sound card and the pci slot 2
2. to allow you to configure the scsi card to do fast-10 scsi

let me know and i will add them also


