I just wanted to add that the make xconfig and make
menuconfig are missing the option to select a image
type. When make config is started a selection must
be given on the alpha used, default something like
alcor. My had to be set to Noname, multia, before a
good bootable image could be generated. So my advice
to you is :
  1) Use make xconfig or make menuconfig to set your
     options followed by;
  2) make config, to select alpha image type. Default
     can just be entered since these are red from the
     previous .config
Start make dep; make boot and a good image will be
generated.





