For perspective, I can tell you that a new PC164LX motherboard which has
533Mhz 21164 processor with 2MB cache, 4 168 pin DIMM slots, 3 ISA ports,
2 32 BIT PCI ports, 2 64 PCI ports, integrated IDE and I/O will cost you
between $1125 and $1400 dollars depending on where you buy it.

As to how well it runs Linux compared to a Pentium: much faster.  Remember
that this is a RISC architecture.  The Pentium is a CISC architecture
which, among other issues, is more or less optimized for the DOS platform
and the Windows application.




