I have diald running on my LX164. Get diald-0.16.5a-1.src.rpm from
Red Hat or a mirror. Execute rpm -ivh diald-0.16.5a-1.src.rpm. Copy
the tar.gz file to someplace along with the patch files. Execute
tar zvf diald-0.16.tar.gz. Enter the diald directory and edit the
following:

1. In the file diald.c, comment out the line
   "SIGNAL(SIGSTKFLT, stray_signal);"

2. In the directory bin, edit the file dctrl after line 242 add the line
   "after 500" (this solves a hang).

3. Look at the Makefile and edit the default directories as desired.

4. make ; make install

The only "problem" is the unaligned traps generated. Diald has been
running without any problem here since October 25.

