Been there, UDB with RedHat 4.2.  This is what I did:
Boot the install, (boot and root disks), tell the install that it is an 
upgrade install and follow it till it detects the harddrive partitions. 
At that point, after it had detected the root partition, I did an 
"Alt-F2" to get to a virtual terminal. If memory serves me, the root
("/")
was mounted under /tmp. "cd" to "/tmp/etc" type "../bin/vi ./passwd" and 
delete the password field for root. Save the changes, the type "sync" a 
few times so the change is written to disk.  Then type "init 0" to
reboot.
This work for me, hope it helps.
-diahedrial.

