steve@dnuk.com wrote:

> Is there a web site on the net that gives information on the Alpha
> architecture, including things like what graphics and sound cards work
> with the motherboards, etc?

I'd go to a (couple of) vendor(s) and have them quote you a complete
system.  (Some say erroneous things like, "IDE doesn't work in alpha
Linux", so go to at least two.)  The most comprehensive list of vendors
I've seen is at http://www.alphalinux.org/ off the hardware page.

Otherwise, these things change very often, and you'll often see posts
like, "I can't get XX to work," followed by "Really?  I've had it working
for months".  A comprehensive list of the type you'd like would be very
difficult to maintain, and would have numerous entries like "Board Y
works but requires this kernel patch and that XFree86 patch", which would
have to be updated with each rev of the kernel and XFree86.  There's not
*quite* enough volunteer manpower in the Linux/alpha community to do this
right.

OTOH, there seems to be enough vendor competition to give you a system
price nearly as good as the sum of the components.

Good luck,

