IIRC, this means the boot/root disk combo you are using is bad.  Try
booting off the CD (if you aren't already; it's way faster when you're
trying various combinations of boot/root disks).  I assume you're
getting to MILO fine and that you've figured out the basic commands.

I can't remember exactly the MILO command to boot from CD, but it's
something like:
boot sr0:<kernel_image>.gz root=/dev/scd0

or somesuch.  The weird thing is the sr0, which is what MILO calls the
cd drive (probably, it tells you what it's called when you do your
first 'ls' in MILO and it prints out all the devices).

I don't have all my written spells handy on how to get this done, so
if you want more info, email and I'll dig them up.

