The problem as I see it is that Intel is ahead in semiconductor process
technology. Imagine, DEC comes out with a new Alpha and it starts on the
.35u process technology. Meanwhile, Intel is shipping massive amounts of
product on a .25u process and are working on .18u production.

Will Intel be out with .18u processors before DEC/Compaq/whoever gets a
21264 into the hands of 3rd party system makers?

Intel can have a lousy architecture and make up for it if they are always
1-2 generations ahead in semiconductor process technology. If Alpha could
catch up with x86 in terms of process technology then it'd be an incredibly
fast chip and the gap between Intel and Alpha in terms of performance would
be enormous.

