I think DEC realized this, which is why they went fabless.  They couldn't
keep up with Intel on fab investment.  Samsung, however, is a giant,
and is busily upgrading their processes to .25 and .18.  DEC also
forced Intel to agree to fab Alphas for DEC.

IBM also has exciting fab capabilities, but I don't know if they'd
be willing to fab alphas, which are direct competitors:  IBM has both
PowerPC and Power3 to worry about.

The unfortunate lateness of the 21264 really hurt DEC's position.
