I found a description to install RH 5.1 on a Jensen at
http://www.home.unix-ag.org/nils/jensen_install.html
and got the same error messages. The aboot from the RH Bootdisk 
expects
the kernel on an ext2 filesystem. 

The second problem that occurs is that the fdisk or disk druid from RH
5.1 does not accept my partitions
created with minlabel.

On my machine after installing RH 5.1 I got sveral memory violations 
and so on.

My way to install:
Using copyboot, minlabel and the diskimages from digital. Using RH 2.1
and RH 5.1

disk1: partition1 4MB boot
             partition2 4MB ext2
             partition3 800 MB ext2 root
             partition4 128 MB swap

disk2: partition1 800 MB linux native
             partition2 128 MB linux swap

1. With ARC console use minlabel to partition disk1. Use copyboot to 
write bootdisk to first sector.
2. Install RH 2.1 on disk1
3. Copy kernel from RH 5.1 on disk1 partition2
4. Using copyboot to write RH 5.1 bootdisk to first sector of disk1
5. Now you are ready to install RH 5.1 on disk2

If you have other systems with linux you can create the second 
partition with ext2 filesystem in this machine
and move the disk to your jensen.
So my way is very strange and I killed my installation because it is 
not stable.

