You seem to have a DU system available to you, with a DEC Fortran compiler.
In that case, you could _compile_ your programs on the DU machine (and
link them statically, unless you have a few more DU library licenses lying
around unused ;-) and _run_ them under linux.

This is what I often do --- I do all the development under linux, using
egcs and the fast maths library, and once I have reached a stable point in
development and want to run the program on large amounts of data, I upload
the source to university, compile under DU, download the executable, and
run the actual (day-long) tests using that code.

