NNTP-Posting-Date: 11 Nov 1998 17:14:01 GMT
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

We have Alphas and PII boxes running RH5.1 and running my code we get a
three fold speed up going from a PII300 to an Alpha 533SX.  The
performance of egcs-1.1 is definitely getting better, the scheduling
looks pretty good to me.  We used to have to manhandle assembly to with
1.03a and that got us around a 30% speed up, now we can barely gain 10%
so we just don't bother anymore, not worth it.  I'm sure the DEC C
compiler could squeeze a little more speed out of the thing but
considering just having a licence for DU would double the price of the
machine I just don't see it being worthwhile.

Its interesting that the people getting the crappiest performance all
seem to be using Fortran.  I wonder if they are doing something
inherently difficult for egcs?

I'm sure this performance issue is not going to go away as long as
people think they can just take any old code and expect the compiler to
do all the work for them, we made some dramatic improvements by fine
tuning our C code.

-- 
Dr. Shane Sturrock - sss@holyrood.ed.ac.uk
