S S Sturrock wrote:

> Its interesting that the people getting the crappiest performance all
> seem to be using Fortran.  I wonder if they are doing something
> inherently difficult for egcs?

Hm, yes and no.
Yes, complex numbers are a major pain for egcs.
Double complex isn't. We learn :
Always use double complex and -fno-emulate-complex ;-)

And no, coz the Dec Fortran compiler is about one the most
unreal things ever. On occasion it beats Dec's C-compiler by quite
a margin (depends as usual on the problem)
(For the  same type of problem, same dimensions etc,
but different languages)
So the standards are somewhat higher on fortran, and this make
fortran/g77 look worse than c/egcs.
The difference is due to pseudo-vectorizing, i.e. pipelining.

Christian







