Actually the chipset (21272,implementing the cross bar switch)
has no heatsink. It's sitting on the motherboard and
can easily be identified (at least in the proto i've had) as a couple of
thin, silver looking chips. The CPU's on the CPU daughterborards have
their own heatsink and on top of it a fan. The other heatsink you may refer
to is also on the CPU daughterboard and is used to cool the power supply
stuff (inverter) on the CPU daughterboard.

