Hi ;-)

Well, this is a hint for all those,
which make use of g77 and complex numbers:

You'll need to do all calculations in double complex.
(No problem, since the alpha is 64 bit anyway)
I haven't found a bug in the actual results yet.
But i stumbled across a cute bug in the code generation:
With -fno-emulate-complex the compiler (egcs-1.1b)
crashes on

write(*,*) some_double_complex_number

So you'll need a workaround for this.
Having done that and having enabled
-fno-emulate-complex
 you get a speedup of a factor 3-4 on complex
code.


Christian







