Greg Lindahl wrote:
> 
> frey@weasel.bme.unc.edu (Eric Frey) writes:
> 
> > This is very cool. I'm a little disappointed that it only has a 83 MHz memory
> > bus (don't most PCs have 100 MHz, albeit the bus is not as wide).
> 
> The LX also has an 83 mhz bus and it's no slouch. The 4 banks on the
> DP board ought to give it an impressive stream.

The LX board has a 66 MHz System Bus (If you don't believe me measure it
at U39-1
if memory serves).
It is however 128 bits wide (plus ECC).

The chip set for the 21264 doesn't use the same clock for memory and
system bus.
The 21264 uses 64 bit unidirectional buses for the system bus and either
256 or
512 bit wide memory (plus ECC).  There is an integer relationship
between the
two clocks though, probably x4 in this case  (system bus at 333 MHz).  I
heard
they were shooting for 350 MHz.



