Robert Hartman <rhartman@gmu.edu> writes:

> 
> Has anyone played with the Alpha port of Debian?  I'm thinking of
> switching to Debian on my 433au from RedHat to avoid the increasing
> amount of gaping security holes associated with RedHat.
> 
> Comments Appreciated!

Well, I follow closely the Debian-Alpha efforts, and to try to
contribute to it, so maybe I can try a few comments:

1) I think security would be a bad motivation to switch:
Most security holes are not specific to one distribution, both Redhat
and Debian try to have a quick response when holes are discovered; and
both usually do a good job (nobody's perfect though).
But Debian-Alpha has not been yet officially released, so there
no specific attention given to security holes in the Alpha porting
effort.

2) On the other hand, there maybe some other valid reasons to try
Debian-Alpha:
- familiarity with Debian on other i386 machines,
- number of packages available in Debian,

3)
Altough the developement distribution has been rock-solid at times,
it is a moving target, and sometimes important things may become broken.
That means you need to follow closely the debian-alpha lists, as long
as the official release is not done (hopefully Alpha port will be
released with Debian 2.1 in December).

Regards,

Loic



