This is some info from Compaq/Digital via the AlphaNT mail list.

>> Pardon the question - what is the bus speed for the new 264DP -
>>21264 combo?
>> I seem to remember some IO discussion from an earlier note.
>
>The main memory consists of two memory "ports", each 256 bits wide running
>at 83.333MHz for a peak bandwidth of ~83M X 32bytes or 2.6 GBytes/sec per
>port.  Each processor to chipset connection is 64 bits wide (data only,
>there are other address and control bits), runs its clock at 2X the memory
>clock and transfers data on both edges of the clock.  so its transfer rate
>is 4X the memory frequency with 1/4 the bus width for the same 2.6 GBytes
>per second per processor port.  Note that since the chipset is structured
as
>a switch and not a bus, each processor can be using one of the memory ports
>at the same time so the aggregate bandwidth in a 2 CPU system is 5.2GBytes
>per second.  This may be a little more detail than you were looking for but
>simply giving a "bus speed" on a system like this would likely generate a
>lot of confusion and discussion on the list.

- mark





