> : Summary: Motherboards with dual 21264's at $7999 per in quantity.
> :          Available January.
> This is very cool. I'm a little disappointed that it only has a 83 MHz memory
> bus (don't most PCs have 100 MHz, albeit the bus is not as wide).

First of all, it's not a bus. CPU, Memory and I/O are all connected to a
crossbar switch. The switch has two memory ports (256b @ 83Mhz) which
theoretically gives the board >5GB/s memory bandwidth. The switch btw
is impemented by the core logic chipset (21272)

> The price
> is a little high. It is equivalent to about 8 PII-450s. Hopefully this price
> will come down and the speed will go up.

Given that according to http://biz.yahoo.com/bw/981102/sun_micros_2.html Sun
intends to charge $4249 for a 400Mhz Ultrasparc II (Quantities 1000), it is not
completely out-of-range and there is a fair chance that prices will come down
over
time. As for speed, those inital chips are still fabricated in .35u, smaller
geometries are
to be expected (allowing higher clock frequencies).

