User-Agent: tin/pre-1.4-980618 (UNIX) (Linux/2.0.35 (i486))
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

I have tried both boards using RedHat 5.1 and I am here to tell you that the
LX is much easier to use.  It has a better BIOS and seems much more stable. 
A colleage and I have just spent an entire day trying to re-install using a
SCSI CD-ROM drive on the UX and getting all sorts of wierd errors (some
whilst still in the BIOS!).  Yes, I have tried to upgrade the BIOS, it
stopped the machine working completely.

I suspect that the main reason that the LX is easier to get on with is that
they are much more common and thus more people have bashed the bugs.

We may well buy some more UX boards, but only because headless (i.e. no
video card) units can be stacked in a rack twice as densely as LX boards
(because they have no expansion cards sticking up).  But we will pay someone
else to have the pain of configuring and maintaining them.  Unless you have
a specialist need like this then I suggest you stick with the LX.  

