post.   I agree with James though.  There should be a
simple switch to have the compiler force an ignore.
The program I was having problems with compiled and ran
fine on several other platforms (IBM/AIX, SGI/IRIS,
SPARC/solaris, INTEL/Linux).  However, it would stop with
a SIGFPE five seconds in on the alpha.  And it wasn't a
divide by zero, it was a underflow of some sort.  Ignoring
the error was fine in this case.  Well, here's  my hack.
