> I want to get to know UNIX en am working with Linux, (on a pentium)
>
> It with 32MB ECC  1.2GB HD Diamond 4MB graphic and AEW64 Sound.
> For $375,-

Sounds pretty good for the money, depending on what you want to do with
it.  For most software for which you have source code, it will be
significantly faster than anything else within about twice the price,
and I'd guess you can't get that much video RAM or that good a sound
card for new machines in that price range.

But be forewarned: a LOT of source code will break on the alpha because
many people are sloppy and assume ints and pointers are the same size.
And there's virtually no commercial software available for Linux-alpha.
So if you want to use WordPerfect and Netscape and the like, and compile
GNOME or KDE or mozilla with everything building right the first time,
you're better off buying a cheap 386-compatible machine.

