Depends on what you're doing- some things will be only trivially faster.  But
things like Goto's matrix multiply are several times faster for LX than SX, so
if you do any dense matrix work then LX is worth the extra expense.

LX also has much better IDE performance in recent kernels (3-4x faster, ~1/4
the CPU load -> about as fast as SCSI-2), but an SX IDE DMA driver is also in
the works...

> Bothe the LX and SX are discontinued right now!

Um, do you mean "discounted"?  I haven't heard about them being discontinued!
Intel and Samsung still make the chips, and Samsung is one of many companies
making the boards, and they started recently enough that I'd have a hard time
believing they're going to stop anytime soon...  I could be wrong, butI don't
think so...

