> I just keep wondering why the performace is so
> embarrassing with respect to this ?

Probably because -femulate-complex is still the default option.  Once
the gcc/egcs back end is fixed with respect to the "native" complex
type, -fno-emulate-complex option can become the default, which might
lead to improvements in performance in complex-using apps.  You can
try the option in the meantime, and might even get lucky and avoid
the code-generation bugs....
