Please note that there is a difference between "not supported" (by Redhat)
and "not able to work." Not supported means that RedHat won't help you if
you have problems, that it is not compiled into the kernel distributed by
RedHat, and no doubt some legal and other issues. However, what works is 
determined by the kernel version, regardless of who
distributes it. From what I can tell, soundcards and modules are both
included in the distribution of 2.0.3x, and seem to work fine, even though
RedHat doesn't support them. A kernel reconfig and compile is needed to 
activate them with the RedHat 5.1 distribution. 

-Bob Rinker



