First (for the next time) I always recommand to do a verify after you burn
the new flash to make sure it's succeeded.

It sounds like you failed to update it :-((, but the AS200 have a emergency
update procedure... some small rom code for cases like this which allows you
to update from floppy if this happens. If I remember correctly, you have to
create a boot floppy with the new firmware (check on dec's ftp server
ftp.digital.com in the firmware directory for doc how to do this) and then
you need to set (or remove) a jumper on the motherboard to boot from this
floppy.

