The issue is not that LX is discontinued, rather that the Intel PCI bridge
chip is discontinued. This chip is also used in UX. Samsung has a large
enough stock of UX built, to last until SP264 is released, however, there are
only a handful of LX left worldwide.

There is talk of the possibility that Samsung will strip this chip off of
currently built UX boards, but that in reality is a long shot.

The only real issue is SRM and/or the lack of SRM on UX.

