Organization: OMNILINK -- your link to the Net
MIME-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

Claude R. CIRBA wrote:
> 
> I used to associate 64 bits with more precision for the
> long doubles, as for the PC the long doubles have a little
> more precision other the doubles.  Could you give me
> some insight on this topic ?
> 
> I bought an AS 200 to check this issue before to choose
> between a real alpha screamer and a dual p2.


NOPE, Unfortunatelly not !! 64 bit is only double precision (Intel long
doubles are 80 bits or ten bytes) and current Alpha has NO *hardware*
support for higher precision, even if the Architecture Specification
defines a (possibly future) extended 128-bit precision type, but there
aren't even software routines for it using the current compilers I know
of.

Regarding max. precision at high speed, Intel, too bad, wins !!


Joachim



