Conrad Sanderson wrote:

> Berk Sensoy <bas7@lemur.phy.duke.edu> wrote:
>
> >       Does anyone have any suggestions as to what would be the best
> >compiler options to optimize (make the fastest at run-time) my code on an
> >Alpha/Linux machine? I have a
> >code that solves a biharmonic PDE by calling a Fortran subroutine.  Our
> >group just acquired an Alpha/Linux and we are trying to figure out how
> >best to opimize its various capabilities vis-a-vis an Intel machine.
>
> -O3 -funroll-all-loops -fexpensive-optimizations
> (may need to add -mieee depending on how the code is written)

>
>
> Getting a decent math library will make the most difference:
>
> http://people.frankfurt.netsurf.de/Joachim.Wesner/
>

My favourite is:

g77 -O3 -funroll-loops -fno-schedule-insns -fschedule-insns2 -o foo.x  foo.f
-lffm -lfm -lm

Our code yields a factor of three on a 533 Mhz linux alpha as compared to a
350 Pentium II,
both egcs-1.1b.
For a real fast code, you'll probably need to handoptimize the inner loops
(cache-blocking, and loop-unrolling by four helps a *lot*)

Christian






